  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Arizona's 4th Congressional District, encompassing parts of Phoenix (Ahwatukee), Tempe, and Chandler, will hold an election on November 3, 2026, to elect its U.S. Representative. Incumbent Democrat Greg Stanton, first elected in 2018 and representing the district since 2023 after redistricting, is seeking re-election. He faces a primary challenge from progressive activist Kai Newkirk on July 21, 2026. On the Republican side, physician Zuhdi Jasser is the sole candidate in the GOP primary. Independent candidates Tisha Benoit and John Fillmore are also running in the No Labels Party primary. The district is rated as Solid Democratic by nonpartisan analysts, making the Democratic primary the key contested race in this cycle.",
  "polling": [],
  "polling_note": "No public opinion polls specific to this race were found as of May 2026. The district is rated Safe D / Solid Democratic by nonpartisan forecasters including The Economist and Cook Political Report.",
