      "name": "Greg Stanton",
      "party": "Democratic Party",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Greg Stanton is the incumbent U.S. Representative for Arizona's 4th Congressional District, first elected in 2018 representing the former 9th district and the 4th district since 2023. He previously served as Mayor of Phoenix from 2012 to 2018 and on the Phoenix City Council for nine years. Stanton serves on the House Transportation and Infrastructure Committee, the Foreign Affairs Committee, and the Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party, and he co-founded the bipartisan Extreme Heat Caucus.",
